WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:04.360
JOE: The use of parental controls
with online media, can solve many

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.930
problems with regards to protecting
children with autism, from

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.020
unpleasant or inappropriate content.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.210
This, however, will probably only work
short term, because the individual may

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:19.379
become more proficient at bypassing these
controls, as they get older, especially

00:00:19.379 --> 00:00:20.789
if they are good with technology.

00:00:21.679 --> 00:00:25.090
Parents may also stop monitoring
the children as they feel that

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.639
there isn’t a need anymore.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:31.470
BETH: Most of the time the use of
IT, video games and social media in

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:36.489
moderation, can be positive activities, as
long as sensible guidelines are followed.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.680
In the same way safety checks
are done when children and young

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.160
people are out and about, then the
same should apply on the internet.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.760
However, when is an individual with
autism, deemed old enough to make

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.839
their own choices and to be trusted
online, should parents still enforce

00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:55.230
their controls on adults because of
a perceived need to protect them?

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.540
JOE: It can be more successful if
parents share internet experiences with

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:03.540
their children, having regular open
discussions with them about their safety

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.780
in general, but especially online.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:10.390
As the internet means so much to many
autistic children, parents taking an

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.399
interest seems natural and supportive and
a way to develop the parent-child bond,

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.869
rather than a way of spying on them.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.569
BETH: Addiction especially can be
a concern for parents of autistic

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:25.170
children and adults, as their
obsessive nature can lead to internet

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.390
gaming and social media dependency.

00:01:27.839 --> 00:01:31.320
An individual with autism may often
find sanctuary from the real world,

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.290
in an alternate world that appears
safe, and offers an opportunity to

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:39.180
meet and communicate comfortably in
their own home with people more like

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.149
themselves, with the same interests.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:45.449
JOE: Many individuals with autism who
suffer loneliness and isolation due

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.509
to problems with social interaction,
can find communicating via a computer

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.960
a much less stressful and a more
enjoyable way of maintaining friendships.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.960
Social media allows for an almost
instant response and can be

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.110
helpful in communicating with
other individuals with autism and

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.020
their families, friends and carers.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.710
BETH: It enables charities and
organisations offering help and

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:11.140
advice to reach people more easily
with online support available often

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.850
24/7, not just during office hours.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.660
The internet can have both positive and
negative impacts on individuals with

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:23.640
autism and their families, however If
used appropriately and in moderation, can

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.480
be of great benefit in terms of offering
a different form of socialisation.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.260
It can also be beneficial in
terms of accessing information

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:33.070
and being able to share interests.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.240
JOE: Negative things can happen using
social media and the internet as they can

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.449
in all aspects of life, but as long as
individuals with autism are made aware

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.350
and prepared for those risks, they can
develop the tools to cope with them.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.880
BETH: The positive thing about
computers and the internet is that

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.280
they are potentially the greatest
asset for individuals with autism,

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:58.049
opening up a new world of potential
friends, opportunity and employment.

00:02:58.639 --> 00:03:03.000
The internet is here to stay so it is
important to make it a positive and

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.350
beneficial experience for all, however
they can most effectively use it.

